## QA & Debugging

During testing, the purchase event was initially firing incorrectly on the product list page.

### Root Cause
The purchase tag relied on a page-based trigger that could evaluate under unintended conditions.

### Resolution
The trigger was redesigned to use:

- Custom Event = purchase
- URL transaction_id validation

This ensured the purchase event only fired after a confirmed transaction.

### Validation
A complete end-to-end user journey was tested:

view_item_list → view_item → add_to_cart → begin_checkout → add_shipping_info → add_payment_info → purchase

All events fired successfully at the correct stage of the checkout funnel.
